<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The Saudi state oil company Saudi Aramco h=
as reported that profits rose by more than a third in the latest quarter de=
spite attacks on its facilities.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The world=E2=80=99s top oil exporter poste=
d a net profit of $3.25bn in the three months to September, compared with $=
26.9bn a year earlier.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The US-Israeli war on Iran has reduced Ara=
mco=E2=80=99s output, but this has been offset by higher oil prices.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">This morning, Brent crude climbed $2.38 a =
barrel to $107.15 a barrel, a 2.2% gain, after <a href=3D"https://ablink.ed=
itorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneH=
EBMPiQQXneH1j-HC6lHqbUOjsXaSbKXDxdV0-DwtIzWg-4k1olXzyADgZ9IKcES_pPAAyA9dJMj=
DsejXjLMZFnOZuVLSuwNm9ny39yVhOBVXcHe8F2tIi8cViT69QeM58KkogC03sQ1O07WLCfUob4=
-M7EEjpk7zH6kbdUYkcanQpdiA1LFAJEHW-4LQoDaUPr4G-huErIFVLdtRQ1JNr0Q93Ib8lxMnP=
YOMl1r6RSB6A/4vf/8Y7bIXuyRIO4kj2VLGvXSA/h32/h001.3cunzPwG_unVkYwShYv6xt6EKB=
1BW83METYD99f4LIA" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">the =E2=81=A0US reportedly lau=
nched limited strikes on =E2=80=8BIran=E2=80=99s Qeshm Island</a> late on M=
onday. (Before the war, which started on 28 February, Brent traded about $7=
2 a barrel.)</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">However on Monday, <a href=3D"https://abli=
nk.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszc=
CSneHEAsxWg7d8sWyUjf1CJIvNP3ipfpVIN_dOTWXDHJBV5WfbEBrJn8mlzd3fwt5xww4DFaBSJ=
NyNRdHbplz2ZaBWvXfwXxC8PmYA8KaDetjltRP8ea4UDcNlDhJXqgSNa-U19yCan-Hrfm-hTjMA=
ODpvktInZJyPHe6RvC_CJq_oBONcUIowyDOgmh7U4YhneL23F7RJVd7GWPuLjTRR3sO1pqPJYLY=
6ef5y0-bTWbfVzzCCR8lQy4FAdYTwmQAa9T7mMHZUMkgkldsMzIkN-ZoWA8/4vf/8Y7bIXuyRIO=
4kj2VLGvXSA/h33/h001.Zo3F4kyqC-5w0lNifVXphCldOxnVNY1cnc0sKZGeIuI" style=3D"=
color: #0077B6;">the global oil benchmark plunged</a> 11% to $103.28 a barr=
el after Donald Trump reportedly said he was willing to give diplomacy more=
 time.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Amin H Nasser, Aramco=E2=80=99s president =
and chief executive, said: =E2=80=9CGeopolitical uncertainty and attacks on=
 key energy facilities continued to amplify the global energy supply crisis=
 in the third quarter of 2026, with serious implications for global energy =
security. Despite challenges, the unwavering dedication of our workforce, o=
ur operational excellence, the flexibility of our system, and the strength =
of a supply network built over decades enabled us to continue delivering re=
liably to our customers through this extraordinary period.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CWe continue to explore additional=
 overseas storage capacity and alternative export routes to further strengt=
hen our global supply network, and our robust operational and financial per=
formance during this volatile period demonstrates the value of our resilien=
ce.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">This means that the world=E2=80=99s bigges=
t oil companies are on track for combined profits of about $100bn between J=
uly and September.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Australia=E2=80=99s central bank has lifte=
d interest rates for the fifth time this year, taking them to the highest l=
evel in 18 years.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The Reserve Bank of Australia=E2=80=99s bo=
ard raised its cash rate by 25 basis points to 4.85% and said it will conti=
nue to do what it considers necessary to bring inflation to target. However=
, it dropped its previous guidance that it would raise the cash rate furthe=
r if needed.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">And a surprisingly narrow 6-3 vote indicat=
ed policymakers may be getting to the end of their rate hikes.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Michele Bullock, the governor, said it was=
 =E2=80=9Cnot the news that many Australians want to hear=E2=80=9D, but it =
would prevent =E2=80=9Ceven worse pain down the track=E2=80=9D.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">She said it was unclear what the next move=
 in rates will be, adding that the three dissenting members stressed downsi=
de risks such as the weakening housing market and rising unemployment.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">After five rate hikes this year, she said =
it is an appropriate time to pause and assess how the economy is responding=
 to the rate rises, but cautioned that =E2=80=9Cthere is still a bit of a s=
kew on the upside to inflation risks, and we need to be alert to those mate=
rialising=E2=80=9D.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Updated forecasts from the central bank sh=
ow headline inflation hitting 4.5% in the fourth quarter, before easing bac=
k to the target range of 2% to 3% in the second half of next year. Unemploy=
ment is forecast to rise above 5% in the next couple of years.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Ipek Ozkardeskaya, senior analyst at Swiss=
quote, said: =E2=80=9CHigher energy prices =E2=80=A6 would strengthen the c=
ase for further monetary policy tightening by the Federal Reserve (Fed) and=
 other major central banks. The Reserve Bank of Australia delivered a 25bp =
hike today, as expected, while the Bank of England (BoE) is widely expected=
 to announce a 25bp hike on Thursday, following a rather uneventful budget =
announcement last week that allows the BoE to go on with its life =E2=80=93=
 and take care of its inflation problem.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9COverall, if we take a step back a=
nd look at the bigger picture, the latest monetary policy decisions have br=
ought either rate hikes or the prospect of tighter monetary policy to fight=
 inflation fuelled by elevated global energy prices. On top of that, many d=
eveloped-market bond yields face upward pressure from intensifying fiscal c=
oncerns, while large bond issuance by technology companies to finance their=
 massive AI buildout could add to that pressure.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The cryptocurrency exchange Binance said h=
ourly deposits exceeded withdrawals this morning, suggesting flows are stab=
ilising after its hack last week. This resulted in $6.3bn of assets being s=
tolen from customer accounts.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">It has been described as the biggest heist=
 in history; experts identified <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguar=
dian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEAsxWg7d8sWyUjf=
1CJIvNP3lrHvvGCfEyTYonvJShFxRCWxTVkUmqEZ3_w8Rfscqk7KcZ4oyf8PSDJZunH2mlYdNtD=
hoZpYKhn3or5ZiVt2nlvXqzrInhe5r-EwXm_nVnFWYyWV1zeJmIETHg3DxV5_egc_42j7KVhqRK=
MRKk9s-gF-sd3qwJwZ_9gF6d8A48RC4t4D6ELoF6m3Rt9JGpiMRsIDRhaae80fH5U1tsFncw/4v=
f/8Y7bIXuyRIO4kj2VLGvXSA/h34/h001.1a1HGq9EKZDZ9lQ_sEKhez4UJQxbwWmd0mCt1AQKG=
0Y" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">North Korea as the probable culprit</a>.</p>
